WEBVTT

1
00:00.120 --> 00:03.550
Dictate into a T3 Code thread, and I follow along.

2
00:03.640 --> 00:05.870
When the agent answers, I read it to you,

3
00:05.920 --> 00:08.590
and you hear the first sound
in under a tenth of a second.

4
00:10.140 --> 00:11.530
Nothing leaves your machine.

5
00:11.580 --> 00:13.930
Sherpa-ONNX handles speech.

6
00:13.980 --> 00:17.170
llama.cpp runs the cleanup on your graphics card,

7
00:17.220 --> 00:18.930
and Phonon is my voice.

8
00:18.980 --> 00:21.390
No cloud and no telemetry.

9
00:22.680 --> 00:26.070
We tuned it on 400 of our own real dictations,

10
00:26.120 --> 00:31.550
all measured on one gaming laptop,
with a Core i9 and an RTX 4070.

11
00:31.940 --> 00:33.830
Cleanup got noticeably more accurate,

12
00:33.880 --> 00:37.910
and the hand-off to me dropped from up to a second
to about 30 milliseconds.
